{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794555020,"nonce":"U6rtKUuvksQGDrJnxUFDlTlycDA=","target":"a879861c6f226734c454473797a405ab3b3f3192c1b81def8bb9fea85cd82878","message":"Feasibility spike, 2026-11-13, Android emulator (arm64-v8a, API 36) with the NDK's clang. The program ran; what is missing is tooling, not the runtime.\n\nWorks:\n- The runtime builds for aarch64-linux-android (libash_std.a, 44.2 MB), but only with `BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS_aarch64_linux_android` pointing at the NDK sysroot; std/build.rs finds no headers on its own.\n- `ash --build --target aarch64-linux-android` writes the AOT object.\n- Linked by hand with the NDK clang (`-lm -ldl`; 10.1 MB executable), pushed with adb and run in `adb shell`: hello world and ten test programs print what the interpreter prints, exit 0.\n\nGaps, each a step of this issue's acceptance list:\n- Items 1 and 2: no NDK discovery and no header discovery.\n- Item 4: `ash --build` stops at the missing link step for the android triple.\n- The deliverable proposed in comment #2 is a library loaded by NativeActivity with `xwindow_main` defined; the spike ran a plain executable, so the glue and the Gradle wiring are untried.\n\nNot tested: threads and fibers, GC under memory pressure, a physical device, HDLL natives (no static binding path yet), armv7 and x86_64.","files":null}]}